## Why This Is Asked

Assesses multi-account isolation, tenant tagging, and rapid containment capabilities in AWS.

## Key Concepts

- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag
- SCPs and cross-account trust boundaries
- Tenant-scoped KMS keys with rotation
- PrivateLink/VPCE for data paths
- Immutable logging and breach-testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// trust policy snippet (conceptual)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate breach containment within 60 seconds end-to-end?
- What telemetry would you rely on for incident attribution?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a secure, cross-account multi-tenant streaming architecture with strict tenant isolation, fine-grained access controls, key management best practices, and rapid incident response capabilities in a production data pipeline context.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account trust relationships with ABAC and MFA enforcement
- Tenant isolation across streaming data paths using account boundaries
- Per-tenant KMS keys with automatic rotation for cryptographic isolation
- PrivateLink/VPC endpoints for private, encrypted data transit without internet exposure
- Immutable audit trails using CloudTrail, S3 Object Lock, and Lake Formation access controls
- Automated breach containment workflow with sub-minute response times

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": ["kinesis:PutRecord", "kinesis:PutRecords"],
    "Resource": "arn:aws:kinesis:*:*:stream/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}/*",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {
        "aws:SourceAccount": "${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}",
        "aws:RequestedRegion": ["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]
      },
      "ArnEquals": {
        "aws:SourceArn": "arn:aws:kinesis:*:*:stream/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}/*"
      },
      "Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"}
    }
  }]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Validates understanding of tenant isolation, least privilege principles, and comprehensive auditing in serverless architectures.

## Key Concepts
- IAM condition-based per-tenant isolation
- CMK encryption with tenant-specific key policies
- DynamoDB partition access patterns by tenant namespace
- CloudTrail immutability for audit integrity
- API Gateway context propagation for tenant identity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example policy snippet (pseudo)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:GetItem","dynamodb:PutItem"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/tenant-data",
      "Condition": {
        "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
          "dynamodb:LeadingKeys": "${aws:userid}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of time-bound access, cross-account trust, and auditable controls for external data sharing in a single AWS account context.

## Key Concepts

- STS AssumeRole with short-lived session
- IAM trust policies and cross-account access
- S3 Access Points and bucket policies for granular prefix access
- TLS enforcement, IP allow-lists, PrivateLink/VPCE
- KMS encryption and CloudTrail/S3 access logs

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_ACCOUNT_ID:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket/your-prefix/*"],
      "Condition": {"IpAddress": {"aws:SourceIp": "203.0.113.0/24"}, "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test and verify revocation works automatically after 14 days?
- What logging and alerting would you add to detect misuse or anomalies?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates expertise in architecting secure, scalable data science environments with strict least-privilege controls across multi-account data lakes, requiring mastery of ABAC, Lake Formation, KMS, and private networking.

## Key Concepts
- Attribute-based access control (ABAC) with IAM policy tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- SageMaker notebook cross-account trust relationships
- Private connectivity through VPC endpoints
- Centralized CMK with rotation policies
- Immutable audit logging via CloudTrail
- Automated drift and privilege-creep detection

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/project}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/dataset": "${aws:PrincipalTag/dataset}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
